IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), PART VII.1, section 152.02: the agreement with the Commission
-- under which this Part applies to a self-employed person, and its termination.
-- Piece ei5, written by the piece agent ei5 (Sonnet 5.5). Layer 1: from the Act's text alone, no point of view.
--
-- The Regulations fix only the form of the notice and of its withdrawal (regs 9.01 and 9.02, piece er1: in
-- writing). They set no circumstances of deemed termination, none that allow termination after benefits have
-- been paid, and no date for a deemed termination (searched for "terminat" in the Regulations, 2026-10-24), so
-- those three facts are plain inputs here; NOTES.md records it as a finding.
-- Dates: no enactment or commencement date in this section.

§ `152.02 Application -- the agreement`

-- src:2146 | 152.02 (1) This Part applies in respect of every self-employed person who is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act who has entered into an agreement with the Commission regarding the application of this Part.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.02(1) (src:2146)
GIVEN `is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has entered into an agreement with the Commission regarding the application of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.02(1) this Part applies in respect of a person` IF
        `is a self-employed person`
    AND (`is a Canadian citizen` OR `is a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act`)
    AND `has entered into an agreement with the Commission regarding the application of this Part`

-- The Commission "may fix the form and the conditions of the agreements": a power of the Commission, to which the
-- person who wants to enter into an agreement is liable. The text does not say what follows when an agreement
-- is not in the form fixed or does not meet a condition (fork F4), so the rule only says whether it does.
-- src:2150 | (3) The Commission may fix the form and the conditions of the agreements.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.02(3) (src:2150)
GIVEN `the Commission has fixed a form and conditions for the agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is in the form fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement meets the conditions fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.02(3) the agreement is in the form and on the conditions the Commission has fixed` IF
        NOT (`the Commission has fixed a form and conditions for the agreements`)
    OR  (`the agreement is in the form fixed` AND `the agreement meets the conditions fixed`)

§§ `152.02 Termination of the agreement (subsections (4) to (7))`

-- What becomes of a notice to terminate. The Act names every outcome, so each is a constructor (no NOTHING).
DECLARE `ei5 What becomes of a notice to terminate an agreement` IS ONE OF
    `ei5 notice - not given in accordance with subsection (4), so the agreement is not terminated by it`
    `ei5 notice - given within 60 days after the agreement was entered into, so the agreement is deemed never to have been entered into`
    `ei5 notice - deemed never to have been given, a benefit period having been established`
    `ei5 notice - withdrawn in the prescribed manner before December 31`
    `ei5 notice - the agreement terminates on December 31 of the year in which the notice was given`

-- Subsection (4), first sentence: the agreement is deemed terminated if any of the circumstances set out in the
-- regulations exists.
-- src:2152 | (4) An agreement is deemed to be terminated if any of the circumstances set out in the regulations exist. It may also be terminated, by notice given to the Commission in the prescribed form and manner, by the individual who entered into it if the notice is given before any benefits are paid to the individual under this Part or, if benefits have been paid under this Part, if any of the prescribed circumstances exist. It may not be terminated in any other manner or at any other time.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.02(4) deemed termination (src:2152)
GIVEN `any of the circumstances set out in the regulations exists` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 152.33(b); no such regulation in the deposited text (pieces er1 to er6)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.02(4) the agreement is deemed to be terminated` IF
    `any of the circumstances set out in the regulations exists`

-- Subsection (4), second and third sentences: the individual may terminate by notice to the Commission in the
-- prescribed form and manner (reg 9.01: in writing), if it is given before any benefits are paid under this Part
-- or, if benefits have been paid, if any of the prescribed circumstances exists. No other manner, no other time.
-- src:2152 | (4) An agreement is deemed to be terminated if any of the circumstances set out in the regulations exist. It may also be terminated, by notice given to the Commission in the prescribed form and manner, by the individual who entered into it if the notice is given before any benefits are paid to the individual under this Part or, if benefits have been paid under this Part, if any of the prescribed circumstances exist. It may not be terminated in any other manner or at any other time.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.02(4) termination by notice (src:2152)
GIVEN `the individual gives notice to the Commission in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 9.01 (piece er1)
      `benefits have been paid to the individual under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of the prescribed circumstances exists` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 152.02(4); no such regulation in the deposited text
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.02(4) the individual may terminate the agreement by notice` IF
        `the individual gives notice to the Commission in the prescribed form and manner`
    AND ((NOT (`benefits have been paid to the individual under this Part`)) OR `any of the prescribed circumstances exists`)

-- Subsection (5): the date of a deemed termination is the prescribed date.
-- src:2154 | (5) If an agreement is deemed to be terminated as a result of circumstances set out in the regulations, the agreement is deemed to be terminated on the prescribed date.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.02(5) (src:2154)
GIVEN `the prescribed date` IS A DATE   -- out of range: s 152.33(b); no such regulation in the deposited text
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 152.02(5) the day on which an agreement deemed to be terminated is terminated` IS
    `the prescribed date`

-- Subsection (6), lead-in: the agreement is terminated on December 31 of the year in which the notice is given.
-- src:2156 | (6) If notice is given to terminate an agreement in accordance with subsection (4), the agreement is terminated on December 31 of the year in which the notice is given unless
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.02(6) (src:2156)
GIVEN `the day on which the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 152.02(6) December 31 of the year in which the notice is given` IS
    YMD (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the notice was given`) 12 31

-- Subsections (6) and (7) together. Subsection (7) opens "Despite subsection (6)", so it is tested first.
--   (7) the notice is given within 60 days after the agreement was entered into: the agreement is deemed never to
--       have been entered into (the 60th day counts: keel fork F4);
--   (6)(a) a benefit period is established for the individual from the day the notice was given to December 31 of
--       that year, both days counted: the notice is deemed never to have been given;
--   (6)(b) the individual withdraws the notice in the prescribed manner before December 31: strictly before;
--   otherwise the agreement terminates on December 31.
-- When both (6)(a) and (6)(b) apply the agreement continues either way; the rule reports (6)(a) (fork F5).
-- src:2156 | (6) If notice is given to terminate an agreement in accordance with subsection (4), the agreement is terminated on December 31 of the year in which the notice is given unless
-- src:2157 | (a) a benefit period is established under this Part for the individual during the period that begins on the date the notice was given and that ends on December 31 of that year, in which case the notice is deemed never to have been given; or
-- src:2158 | (b) the individual withdraws the notice in the prescribed manner before December 31 of the year in which the notice was given.
-- src:2159 | Exception
-- src:2160 | (7) Despite subsection (6), if the notice is given within 60 days after the agreement was entered into, the agreement is deemed never to have been entered into.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.02(6) and (7) (src:2156-2160)
GIVEN `the notice was given in accordance with subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the agreement was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day on which a benefit period was established under this Part for the individual` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the individual withdrew the notice in the prescribed manner` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `ei5 What becomes of a notice to terminate an agreement`
DECIDE `s 152.02(6) and (7) what becomes of a notice to terminate the agreement` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the notice was given in accordance with subsection (4)`)
            THEN `ei5 notice - not given in accordance with subsection (4), so the agreement is not terminated by it`
        IF `the notice was given within 60 days after the agreement was entered into`
            THEN `ei5 notice - given within 60 days after the agreement was entered into, so the agreement is deemed never to have been entered into`
        IF `a benefit period was established between the notice and December 31`
            THEN `ei5 notice - deemed never to have been given, a benefit period having been established`
        IF `the notice was withdrawn before December 31`
            THEN `ei5 notice - withdrawn in the prescribed manner before December 31`
        OTHERWISE `ei5 notice - the agreement terminates on December 31 of the year in which the notice was given`
    WHERE
        `December 31 of the year in which the notice was given` MEANS `s 152.02(6) December 31 of the year in which the notice is given` `the day on which the notice was given`
        `the notice was given within 60 days after the agreement was entered into` MEANS
                `the day on which the notice was given` AT LEAST `the day on which the agreement was entered into`
            AND `the day on which the notice was given` AT MOST `the last day of` 60 `days after` `the day on which the agreement was entered into`
        `a benefit period was established between the notice and December 31` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which a benefit period was established under this Part for the individual`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST d THEN d AT LEAST `the day on which the notice was given` AND d AT MOST `December 31 of the year in which the notice was given`
        `the notice was withdrawn before December 31` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the individual withdrew the notice in the prescribed manner`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST w THEN w AT LEAST `the day on which the notice was given` AND w LESS THAN `December 31 of the year in which the notice was given`

-- The day on which the agreement terminates, if it does. A deemed termination (5) and a notice (6) can both be
-- present; the text does not say which governs, and an agreement ends once, so the earlier day is taken (fork F5).
-- src:2152 | (4) An agreement is deemed to be terminated if any of the circumstances set out in the regulations exist. It may also be terminated, by notice given to the Commission in the prescribed form and manner, by the individual who entered into it if the notice is given before any benefits are paid to the individual under this Part or, if benefits have been paid under this Part, if any of the prescribed circumstances exist. It may not be terminated in any other manner or at any other time.
-- src:2153 | Date of termination
-- src:2154 | (5) If an agreement is deemed to be terminated as a result of circumstances set out in the regulations, the agreement is deemed to be terminated on the prescribed date.
-- src:2155 | Date of termination
-- src:2156 | (6) If notice is given to terminate an agreement in accordance with subsection (4), the agreement is terminated on December 31 of the year in which the notice is given unless
-- src:2157 | (a) a benefit period is established under this Part for the individual during the period that begins on the date the notice was given and that ends on December 31 of that year, in which case the notice is deemed never to have been given; or
-- src:2158 | (b) the individual withdraws the notice in the prescribed manner before December 31 of the year in which the notice was given.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.02(4) to (6) (src:2152-2158)
GIVEN `the agreement is deemed to be terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which an agreement deemed to be terminated is terminated` IS A DATE
      `what became of the notice` IS A `ei5 What becomes of a notice to terminate an agreement`
      `the day on which the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 152.02(4) to (6) the day on which the agreement terminates` IS
    IF `the agreement is deemed to be terminated`
    THEN (IF `the notice ends the agreement` AND `December 31 of the year in which the notice was given` LESS THAN `the day on which an agreement deemed to be terminated is terminated`
          THEN JUST `December 31 of the year in which the notice was given`
          ELSE JUST `the day on which an agreement deemed to be terminated is terminated`)
    ELSE (IF `the notice ends the agreement` THEN JUST `December 31 of the year in which the notice was given` ELSE NOTHING)
    WHERE
        `December 31 of the year in which the notice was given` MEANS `s 152.02(6) December 31 of the year in which the notice is given` `the day on which the notice was given`
        `the notice ends the agreement` MEANS
            `what became of the notice` EQUALS `ei5 notice - the agreement terminates on December 31 of the year in which the notice was given`

-- Subsection (2): the agreements are of indefinite duration, subject to (4) to (7). So an agreement is in force from
-- the day it was entered into until the day on which it terminates (it is not in force on that day or after: the
-- text says it is "terminated on" that day, fork F6), and an agreement deemed never to have been entered into
-- (subsection (7)) was never in force.
-- src:2148 | (2) Subject to subsections (4) to (7), the agreements are of indefinite duration.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.02(2) (src:2148)
GIVEN `the day on which the agreement was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the agreement is deemed never to have been entered into` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the agreement terminates, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.02(2) the agreement is in force on a day` IF
        NOT (`the agreement is deemed never to have been entered into`)
    AND `the day in question` AT LEAST `the day on which the agreement was entered into`
    AND `the day in question is before the day on which the agreement terminates`
    WHERE
        `the day in question is before the day on which the agreement terminates` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the agreement terminates, if it has`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST t THEN `the day in question` LESS THAN t
